{
  "dom_id": "step-q212906",
  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "The United States Declaration of Independence was ratified on July 4th, 1776. Given that January 1st, 1776, was a Monday, use congruences to determine on which day of the week the Declaration of Independence was ratified.\n\n*Hint: The year 1776 was a leap year since it's divisible by $4$ and is not an end-of-century year.*",
  "worked_solution": "We can solve this problem using modular arithmetic.\n\nFirst, we note the number of complete months between January 1st, 1776, and July 1st, 1776. \n\n- There were $3$ months with $31$ days (January, March, and May).\n\n- There were $2$ months with $30$ days (April, and June).\n\n- There was $1$ month with $29$ days (February) since it was a leap year.\n\nTherefore, the number of days $d$ between January 1st and July 4th is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\overset{\\text{days to July 1st}}{\\overset{⏞}{31(3)+30(2)+29(1)}}+3.\n$$\n\nNow, note that\n\n$$\n31≡3,\\,30≡2,\\,29≡1,\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7).\n$$\n\nTherefore, writing the number $d$ modulo $7,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =3(31)+2(30)+1(29)+3 \\\\  & ≡3(3)+2(2)+1(1)+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡9+4+1+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡2+4+1+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡10\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,7) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the day of the week is the same as the date $3$ days after January 1st, 1776, namely Thursday.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
